PARITY NOTES (web source -> native)
------------------------------------------------------------
States reproduced (every one renders, never a blank box):
  loading (skeleton chrome) / empty ("No safety events recorded" ContentUnavailableView) /
  error (QueryError-equivalent + Retry) / content (3 StatCards + event feed) /
  stale (freshness chip + reconnecting banner) / offline (cached + offline banner).
  + defensive compact (cols<=1) layout retained from the web source, though the registry
    min size (2×4) keeps it out of the production grid (clamp guarantees cols>=2).
Data sources bound via P1/S8 state-holder seam (SafetySource); no HTTP in the view:
  useSafetyHistory + useVehicles + useVehicleSystems + useTranslation -> SafetyUpdate snapshots.
Shared components mapped: @/components/data-display StatCard -> SafetyStatTile;
  @/components/feedback EmptyState -> ContentUnavailableView / SafetyEmptyFeed.
Charts/maps: none in source -> none added.
i18n: 40 catalog keys (table "SafetyHistoryWidget"); 100% of code-referenced keys resolve
  through the P1/S10 facade — zero hardcoded English literals in the views. All extracted
  source strings present (the web's single `widget.noSafetyEvents` key with two fallbacks is
  preserved as widget.noSafetyEvents "No safety events" + widget.noSafetyEventsRecorded
  "No safety events recorded" so neither extracted string is lost).
Accessibility: VoiceOver labels on stats row, every event row, freshness chip, refresh /
  open / retry controls; Dynamic Type via tokenized fonts; high-contrast via dynamic tokens.
Telemetry: SafetyModel.start() emits the P1/S11 view.opened event with surface slug
  "SafetyHistoryWidget" exactly once (asserted).

